<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">28 January in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 28 January, from 814 to 1986.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charlemagne.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">814 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,212 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charlemagne dies at Aachen</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Frankish king, crowned emperor in 800, died after ruling much of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. His empire was divided among his grandsons within thirty years, but its memory shaped the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aachen">Aachen</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1069">1069 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">957 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Robert de Comines, Earl of Northumbria, is killed at Durham</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Robert de Comines, briefly Earl of Northumbria, was killed in Durham. His violent death was one of the key events that led to the Harrying of the North, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-the-conqueror">William the Conqueror</a>'s campaigns of 1069–1070 to subjugate northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-the-conqueror">William the Conqueror</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durham-england">Durham</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1547">1547 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">479 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry VIII dies at Whitehall</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII</a> died aged 55 after a reign that broke with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, dissolved the monasteries and saw six marriages. His nine-year-old son succeeded him as Edward VI.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1613">1613 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">413 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Galileo observes Neptune without recognising it</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galileo-galilei">Galileo</a>'s notes record a 'star' near Jupiter that was in fact <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neptune">Neptune</a>, and even note that it seemed to move. The planet was not identified until 1846.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1807">1807 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">219 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gas lamps light Pall Mall in London</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Frederick Albert Winsor's demonstration lit part of Pall Mall with gas lamps, the first public street lighting by gas. Gas lighting spread rapidly through British cities over the next decades.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1871">1871 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">155 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Paris capitulates and France signs an armistice with Germany</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a four-month siege, the French government agreed an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armistice-of-11-november-1918">armistice</a> with the new <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a>. The peace that followed cost <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace">Alsace</a> and much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/german-empire">German Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1932">1932 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">94 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Japanese forces attack Shanghai</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Japanese marines clashed with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/19th-route-army">19th Route Army</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shanghai">Shanghai</a>, and Japanese aircraft bombed the Zhabei district. The fighting lasted over a month before a ceasefire was brokered.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1986">1986 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">40 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Space Shuttle Challenger breaks apart after launch</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Challenger broke apart 73 seconds after lift-off, killing its seven crew, including teacher Christa McAuliffe. A faulty seal in a booster rocket was to blame, and shuttle flights stopped for 32 months.</p></div></li></ol>
